  "answer_text": "Here is a complete overview of the **MLA and MP seats in Telangana**:\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f MLA Seats (State Legislative Assembly)\n\n- There are **119 MLAs** in the Telangana Legislative Assembly, elected by the people. The state is divided into **119 constituencies** with roughly equal populations.\n\n- The Telangana Legislative Assembly came into existence with 119 seats in **June 2014** with the formation of Telangana.\n\n- The members of the Vidhan Sabha are directly elected by the people through adult franchise, with each constituency electing one member.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdf\ufe0f MP Seats (Lok Sabha / Parliament)\n\n- Telangana has **17 Lok Sabha constituencies**, with **3 reserved for Scheduled Castes (SC)** and **2 for Scheduled Tribes (ST)**, where electors participate in direct elections to choose their preferred candidates for the position of Member of Parliament (MP).\n\n- The state has **17 Lok Sabha** and **7 Rajya Sabha** seats.\n\n---\n\n## \ud83c\udfdb\ufe0f Legislative Council (MLC Seats)\n\n- The Telangana Legislative Council consists of **40 members**, of whom 14 are elected by members of the Telangana Legislative Assembly, 14 by the local authorities of the state, 6 are nominated by the Governor, 3 are elected by teachers of the state, and 3 are elected by graduates of the state.\n\n---\n\n### \ud83d\udcca Quick Summary Table\n\n| House | Seats |\n|---|---|\n| MLA (Vidhan Sabha) | **119** |\n| MP (Lok Sabha) | **17** |\n| MP (Rajya Sabha) | **7** |\n| MLC (Legislative Council) | **40** |",
